    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1661">

                <pb facs="1357" n="1241" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100 K77/224.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Panama to the Assistant Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Panama</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have had the pleasure
                    of receiving your very courteous communication of the 13th instant by which you
                    are pleased to inform me that [etc.]</p>
                <p>No sooner had your very kind letter reached my hands than I communicated by cable
                    with my Government announcing to it the intended visit of Secretary Knox to our
                    capital, which intelligence, I am sure, has been received by my Government and
                    the people of Panama with positive satisfaction; and I am anxiously looking
                    forward to notice of the precise date on which the visit will be made so as to
                    report it to my Government and enable it to make preparations for the reception
                    due to so distinguished a guest.</p>
                <p>I sincerely appreciate the flattering assurance, you are pleased to communicate
                    to me in behalf of Mr. Knox regarding his impressions upon his visit to Panama,
                    and I am glad to assure you for my part that my country will feel highly honored
                    at having, although for a short time unfortunately, the Secretary of State of
                    this great nation with us.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ricardo Arias.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
